 Board Member (ISD #2753) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #2753) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Renee Kreemer","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"David Ruda","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Jeremiah Zahnow","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Marja Krueger","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Long Prairie-Grey Eagle","schoolNum":"2753"}],"referendums":[{"id":"mn-amendment-1","name":"CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT 1: Increasing funding to school districts","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Minnesota Constitution be amended to increase the funding going to all school districts from the permanent school fund, which is a fund that supports school districts without raising individual income or property taxes, effective July 1, 2027?"},{"id":"mn-todd-08272-township-question-1-bruce-twp","name":"TOWNSHIP QUESTION 1 (Bruce Twp): Shall Bruce Township Adopt New Terms for Supervisors","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Starting in 2027 shall the Town of Bruce establish 6 year terms for Supervisors?","mcds":["08272"]},{"id":"mn-todd-08668-township-question-1-burleene-twp","name":"TOWNSHIP QUESTION 1 (Burleene Twp): Option D - Abandon Clerk/Treasurer Position","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall option D, providing for combining the offices of clerk/treasurer, be abandoned for the government of the town?","mcds":["08668"]},{"id":"mn-todd-08668-township-question-2-burleene-twp","name":"TOWNSHIP QUESTION 2 (Burleene Twp): Option B - Appointment of Clerk and Treasurer Position","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall option B, providing for the appointment of one clerk and one treasurer by the town board, be adopted for the government of the town?\n\nNote - Approval of the Option B question #2 is contingent on the simultaneous approval of Option D question #1","mcds":["08668"]},{"id":"mn-todd-sd0743-school-district-question-1-isd-743","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #743): Renewal of Expiring Capital Project Levy   To Fund Technology","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 743 (Sauk Centre Public Schools) has proposed a capital project levy authorization of 2.281% times the net tax capacity of the school district. This authorization would renew the school districts existing authorization which is scheduled to expire after taxes payable in 2027. The proposed capital project levy authorization will raise approximately $388,061 for taxes payable in 2028, the first year it is to be levied, and would be authorized for ten years.  The estimated total cost of the projects to be funded over that time period is approximately $3,880,610. The additional revenue from the proposed capital project levy authorization will provide funds for the acquisition, installation, replacement, support and maintenance of software, software licenses, computers, improved technology equipment, networks, infrastructure, and the costs of technology related personnel and training.\n\nShall the capital project levy authorization proposed by the school board by Independent School District No.743be approved?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING TO RENEW AN EXISTING CAPITAL PROJECTS REFERENDUM THAT IS SCHEDULED TO EXPIRE.","schoolNum":"0743","area":"Sauk Centre"}]}